{
  "$comment": [
    "M3 AC-12 / grill F-1: the single source of truth for record-validation rules, consumed by BOTH suites.",
    "xUnit reads it in ValidationContractTests.cs (BEHAVIOR-m3-backend-api-031); vitest reads it in",
    "src/domain/validationFixtureContract.test.ts. The C# validator therefore cannot pass its own opinion of the",
    "rules, and neither can the client's.",
    "Rows were authored FROM src/domain/validation.ts and the spec's sections 4.1/4.3, not from what anyone believes",
    "the rules should be. Where the two sides differ, expect differs per side and why names the document that grants",
    "the difference. `violations` is the expectation for a rejecting side; `clientViolations`/`apiViolations`",
    "override it for one side alone, used only where both reject but not the same fields.",
    "the difference. Add a rule by adding rows, never by adding a branch to one validator alone."
  ],
  "violationsFormat": "A rejecting side must report exactly these violations, in order, by field and message text.",
  "counting": "Lengths are UTF-16 code units: JavaScript String.length and .NET string.Length agree; Python len() does not.",
